  "lead_analysis": [
    "Graph statistics match COLMAP at 2.5k (22930 vs 22801 points, 593k vs 612k observations, all 2500 images in one model), so the loop, triangulation and filtering reproduce COLMAP's structure.",
    "Trajectory accuracy does not: ATE 0.344 m vs 0.072 m, Sim(3) scale 1.219 vs 1.026, with error spread uniformly over all ten segments (0.20-0.39 m) rather than growing, i.e. a global metric/shape error, nearly identical to the legacy generalized_rig_sfm result (0.32 m) on the same graph.",
    "The remaining common factor is the optimizer: the T265 baseline (~6 cm) makes metric scale a weakly observable direction; Ceres in COLMAP iterates until the gradient max-norm is below 1e-4, whereas the legacy bundle.rs LM stops on relative cost change 1e-6 (or the iteration cap) and never fully resolves that direction. Second candidate: the 6-point DLT generalized PnP versus GP3P.",
    "Next: rerun 2.5k with the native BA (C2.5, Ceres-style LM with gradient tolerance) before touching anything else; if scale converges to ~1.03 the optimizer explanation holds, otherwise proceed to C3 (GP3P) and a per-frame pose diff against COLMAP's registration log.",
